From 9523325aeab07412b7c0e5960ddbb331f83f135e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:22:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Fix out-of-bounds timestamp metadata read

When no queued input buffer matches the timestamp of a decoded buffer,
iris_get_ts_metadata() falls back to inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].
metadata_idx is the next slot to be written and is only wrapped before
the next write, so after 64 input buffers it equals ARRAY_SIZE(tss) and
the fallback reads past the end of the array. The bytes found there are
ORed into the capture buffer flags, which can set V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST:
userspace then sees a spurious EOS event and every following DQBUF
fails with -EPIPE.

Even within bounds the entry belongs to an unrelated frame, so do not
copy any metadata when there is no match.

Seen on SM8475 with VP9 streams containing hidden frames, whose empty
capture buffers carry no input timestamp.

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
index 246ad0abb..04bb91299 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -928,9 +928,13 @@ static void iris_get_ts_metadata(struct iris_inst *inst, u64 timestamp_ns,
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * No input buffer carried this timestamp (for example an empty buffer
+	 * returned for a frame that is not shown). metadata_idx is the next
+	 * slot to write and can be one past the end of tss[], so there is no
+	 * metadata to copy.
+	 */
 	vbuf->flags &= ~mask;
-	vbuf->flags |= inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].flags;
-	vbuf->timecode = inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].tc;
 }
 
 int iris_vb2_buffer_done(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_buffer *buf)
-- 
2.55.0

